  "title": "National Grid volunteers support conservation efforts at Gunpowder Park",
  "summary": "Working with members of the local community, the team helped improve the local landscape by removing old barbed wire fencing that had become a hazard, clearing overgrown vegetation to restore the meadow, and cutting back hedgerows as part of wider habitat management.A thunderstorm may have paused proceedings for a short time, but the team and local volunteers pulled together and continued their efforts throughout the afternoon, completing all the planned activities.Alison Cormack, Community Liaison Officer said:",
